+## Flow-compression S9 promotions (2026-10-25)
+
+Source: workstream flow-compression, phases 1-7, distilled in phase 8 plan 08-01 from the eight incident files
+`vault/incidents/2026-10-2*-flow-compression-*.md`. Each promotion below was preceded by a recorded grep of this file
+(the grep log is in 08-01-SUMMARY.md); a candidate already covered at equal or greater strength is linked under
+"Evaluated, not promoted", not duplicated.
+
+### Process Rules
+
+**`PR-SEAL-IS-CLOSED-WHEN-THE-SCHEDULER-AGREES-001`** -- A phase or unit of work is sealed only when the reader that decides
+what runs next reports it complete, never when the writer's artifact exists. Phases 1-4 of this mission were sealed and
+closed by hand twice while `init.progress` still counted them incomplete, so the scheduler would have re-run them.
+Fix: assert the reader's count advanced (`completed_count` and per-phase `phase_complete` from `init.progress`), and
+put that assertion in the seal's own test, not in a note.
+Evidence: `vault/incidents/2026-10-24-flow-compression-phase-seal-without-frontmatter.md`; commits `89fa5527`, `b9ff692d`;
+measured `completed_count` 7 at 2026-10-25T11:23:04Z by `tools/s9_kv_check.py` (`check: init-progress`).
+
+**`PR-INFERRED-FIGURE-PRINTS-ITS-BASIS-001`** -- A number copied between documents carries its basis (measured, inferred,
+carried unchanged, assumed) and its denominator, or it reads as measured. Measured in S7: a carried-unchanged idle figure
+read as a gain, a 7-gap summary figure stood against 66 gaps in the regenerated report, and a 27,484 mission-hour headline
+was about 94 percent unobserved time. This is distinct from `PR-FIXTURE-IS-ORACLE-POPULATION-001`, which is about an
+oracle's input population, not a printed figure's label.
+Fix: the report writer refuses an untagged number or empty tag; unmeasured is kept apart from zero; a figure quoted in a
+second document is regenerated from its source.
+Evidence: `vault/incidents/2026-10-25-flow-compression-figure-without-basis.md`; commits `9bf8cd9a`, `25dca5f5`, `c1d17703`;
+gates `V-S7-REPORT-TAGGED`, `V-S7-IDLE-BEFORE-AFTER` in `tools/test_s7_replay.py`.
+
+### Traps
+
+**`T-DRILL-WITHOUT-A-NOOP-CONTROL-001`** -- A mutation drill whose harness was never shown to read a non-failure cannot
+tell a killed mutant from a crashed run or an absent gate. The clean-copy baseline (`T-DRILL-VERDICT-WITHOUT-CONTROL-001`)
+proves the gate passes unmutated; it does not prove the drill reports "not killed" when the mutation changes nothing.
+Measured in S6 and S7: the drill matrix read green before a no-op mutation was driven through it, and a probe that crashed
+on re-run made its gates absent and falsely red in every drill.
+Fix: drive a no-op mutation through the drill and require "survived", assert the real file is untouched afterwards, and
+count "absent" and "crashed" as neither red nor killed (`T-A-CRASH-UNDER-A-MUTANT-COUNTED-AS-A-KILL-001`).
+Evidence: `vault/incidents/2026-10-24-flow-compression-control-never-shown-to-fire.md`; commits `755a757a`, `f1ef65fb`,
+`70f5a2dd`; gates `V-S6-DRILL-CONTROL-NOOP-FIRES` in `tools/test_s6_blockers.py`, `V-S7-DRILL-CONTROL-NOOP-FIRES` and
+`V-S7-DRILL-REAL-FILE-UNTOUCHED` in `tools/test_s7_replay.py`.
+
+### Hard Rule CANDIDATE (NOT registered; not in the compiled hard-rule set)
+
+**`HR-CANDIDATE-SEAL-ASSERTS-THE-READERS-COUNT`** -- STATUS: CANDIDATE pending a second production seal. A phase seal is
+declared only after the scheduler's own completion count is read back and shown to have advanced; the existence of the
+VERIFICATION or SUMMARY file is not that proof.
+Fix: `tools/s9_kv_check.py` `check: init-progress`. Evidence: the phase-seal incident above. Not registered: no
